/-!
# Parasiticity of the kernel and cokernel of a sectionwise isomorphism

Let `B` be a big fppf site, `S` a scheme below its cutoff and `φ : ℱ ⟶ 𝒢` a morphism of sheaves
of `𝒪`-modules on `(Sch/S)_fppf` which is an isomorphism on sections over every object of the
site flat and locally of finite presentation over `S`.  Then the kernel and the cokernel of `φ`
are parasitic for the fppf topology, and therefore

  `H^p(U, ℱ) → H^p(U, 𝒢)`

is bijective for every `U` flat and locally of finite presentation over `S` and every `p`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_flatLocallyOfFinitePresentation_refinement`: a covering sieve of an
  object flat and locally of finite presentation over `S` contains an fppf covering family whose
  members are again flat and locally of finite presentation over `S`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.flat_locallyOfFinitePresentation_of_bigFppfOver_isCovering`: a member of a
  selected covering of `S` itself is flat and locally of finite presentation over `S`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.isParasiticFor_kernel_of_isIso_sections` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.isParasiticFor_cokernel_of_isIso_sections`: the kernel, resp. the cokernel,
  of such a `φ` is `AlgebraicGeometry.IsParasiticFor` the fppf coverings of `S`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.bigFppfCohomology_map_bijective_of_isIso_sections`: the resulting
  comparison of cohomology, the step of [Stacks, Tag 0756] resting on [Stacks, Tag 0755] with
  the parasitic hypotheses **discharged**.

## Implementation notes

The kernel is the easy half: kernels of sheaves of modules are computed on sections, because
`SheafOfModules.toSheaf`, `CategoryTheory.sheafToPresheaf` and evaluation at an object all
preserve finite limits, so the sections of `Ker φ` over `U` are the kernel of `φ` on sections
over `U`, which is zero as soon as `φ` is a monomorphism there.

The cokernel is *not* computed on sections — `CategoryTheory.sheafToPresheaf` preserves no
colimits — and that is where the topology enters.  The quotient map `𝒢 ⟶ Coker φ` is an
epimorphism of sheaves, hence locally surjective
(`CategoryTheory.Sheaf.isLocallySurjective_iff_epi'`), so a section of `Coker φ` over `U` is, on
a covering of `U`, the image of a section of `𝒢`.  Over a member of that covering on which `φ`
is surjective on sections the section of `𝒢` is itself an image, and `ℱ ⟶ 𝒢 ⟶ Coker φ` is zero;
so the original section is locally zero, hence zero, `Coker φ` being a sheaf.  The statement
that makes the covering usable is
`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_flatLocallyOfFinitePresentation_refinement`: a covering sieve of an
object flat and locally of finite presentation over `S` contains an fppf covering family whose
members are again flat and locally of finite presentation over `S`.  It is proved from the
identification of `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.topology` with the Grothendieck topology
generated by the fppf precoverage of schemes pulled back along
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.toScheme`, for which
`CategoryTheory.Precoverage.mem_toGrothendieck_iff_of_isStableUnderComposition` extracts the
refining family.

The cokernel argument is carried out for abelian sheaves
(`AlgebraicGeometry.subsingleton_cokernel_val_obj_of_surjective`) and transported to sheaves of
modules by `CategoryTheory.Limits.PreservesCokernel.iso`: it never mentions the ring sheaf, and
keeping it at the abelian level avoids moving between the sections of a sheaf of modules and the
sections of its underlying abelian sheaf inside a single term.

The members of a *selected* covering of `S` itself are flat and locally of finite presentation
over `S`, which turns the vanishing on all such objects into
`AlgebraicGeometry.IsParasiticFor`, the hypothesis that
`AlgebraicGeometry.bigFppfCohomology_map_bijective_of_isParasiticFor` consumes.

**What this does and does not say about [Stacks, Tag 0756].**  The source's hypotheses are that
`𝒢|_{S_τ}` be quasi-coherent and that `g^*_{τ,small}(𝒢|_{S_τ}) → 𝒢|_{U_τ}` be an isomorphism for
every flat, locally finitely presented `g : U → S`; its `ℱ` is the pullback of `𝒢|_{S_τ}` to
`(Sch/S)_fppf` and `φ` the canonical comparison map.  Read at the identity chart of `U_τ`,
hypothesis (2) says exactly that `φ` is an isomorphism on sections over `U`, and the source's
proof uses (1) and (2) in no other way: that is the hypothesis carried here.  The morphism `φ` is
an arbitrary one in *this* file; the source's own pair `(ℱ, φ)` is constructed in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Descent.Parasitic.FlatCohomologyCounit`, as
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.zariskiComparisonModule` with
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.zariskiComparisonMap` at `τ = Zar` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.etaleComparisonModule` with
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.etaleComparisonMap` at `τ = étale`, where the statement below is
instantiated at it.  The identification of `H^p(U, ℱ)` with the
small-site cohomology `H^p(U, 𝒢|_{U_τ})` by [Stacks, Tag 03DW], which is the conclusion of the
tag, is **not** asserted here; at `τ = Zar` and `U = S` it is
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.zariskiSmallSiteCohomologyAddEquiv`
(`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Descent/Parasitic/FlatCohomologySmallSiteComparison.lean`), and
for a general `U` it is not available.  See the module
documentation of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Descent/Parasitic/FlatCohomologyComparison.lean`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0756](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0756)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0755](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0755)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 06ZL](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/06ZL)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe u w

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-! ### A covering sieve refined by flat, locally finitely presented objects -/

section Precoverages

variable (B : AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)

/-- The fppf precoverage of schemes, pulled back to the big fppf category over `S`. -/
private abbrev overFppfPrecoverage : Precoverage (AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver B S hS) :=
  Scheme.fppfPrecoverage.comap (AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS)

private instance : HasPullbacks B.Schemes :=
  hasLimitsOfShape_of_closedUnderLimits WalkingCospan (fun X : Scheme.{u} ↦ X.size < B.cutoff)

/-- **The topology of `(Sch/S)_fppf` is generated by the pulled-back fppf precoverage.**  The
selected coverings of a big fppf site generate the same topology as all fppf coverings, and
localizing a generated topology at an object generates the localized precoverage. -/
private theorem overFppfPrecoverage_toGrothendieck :
    (overFppfPrecoverage B S hS).toGrothendieck =
      AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.topology B S hS := by
  calc (overFppfPrecoverage B S hS).toGrothendieck
      = ((Scheme.fppfPrecoverage.comap B.inclusion).comap
          (AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.forget B S hS)).toGrothendieck := by
        rw [← Precoverage.comap_comp]
    _ = (B.precoverage.comap
          (AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.forget B S hS)).toGrothendieck := by
        rw [← bigFppfPrecoverage_eq_comap B]
    _ = B.topology.over (B.obj hS) := by
        rw [← CategoryTheory.over_toGrothendieck_eq_toGrothendieck_comap_forget]
    _ = AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.topology B S hS := rfl

/-- The legs of a family in the pulled-back fppf precoverage are flat and locally of finite
presentation. -/
private theorem flat_lfp_leg_of_mem_overFppfPrecoverage
    {X : AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver B S hS} {R : Presieve X}
    (hR : R ∈ overFppfPrecoverage B S hS X) {Y : AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver B S hS}
    (f : Y ⟶ X) (hf : R f) :
    Flat ((AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map f) ∧
      LocallyOfFinitePresentation
        ((AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map f) := by
  rw [Precoverage.mem_comap_iff, Scheme.fppfPrecoverage_eq_inf] at hR
  exact ⟨hR.1.2 (R.map_map hf), hR.2.2 (R.map_map hf)⟩

/-- **Composing with the structure morphism.**  If `f : Y ⟶ X` is flat and locally of finite
presentation and `X` is flat and locally of finite presentation over `S`, then so is `Y`. -/
private theorem flat_lfp_of_comp
    {X Y : AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver B S hS} (f : Y ⟶ X)
    (hf : Flat ((AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map f) ∧
      LocallyOfFinitePresentation ((AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map f))
    (hX : Flat ((Over.post B.inclusion).obj X).hom ∧
      LocallyOfFinitePresentation ((Over.post B.inclusion).obj X).hom) :
    Flat ((Over.post B.inclusion).obj Y).hom ∧
      LocallyOfFinitePresentation ((Over.post B.inclusion).obj Y).hom := by
  have hcomp : (AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map f ≫
      ((Over.post B.inclusion).obj X).hom = ((Over.post B.inclusion).obj Y).hom := by
    show B.inclusion.map f.left ≫ B.inclusion.map X.hom = B.inclusion.map Y.hom
    rw [← Functor.map_comp, Over.w f]
  rw [← hcomp]
  exact ⟨MorphismProperty.comp_mem (@Flat.{u} : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u}) _ _ hf.1 hX.1,
    MorphismProperty.comp_mem
      (@LocallyOfFinitePresentation.{u} : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u}) _ _ hf.2 hX.2⟩

/-- **Every covering sieve of an object flat and locally of finite presentation over `S`
contains an fppf covering family by objects flat and locally of finite presentation over `S`.**

The topology of `(Sch/S)_fppf` is generated by the pulled-back fppf precoverage, so a covering
sieve contains a family of that precoverage; the legs of such a family are flat and locally of
finite presentation, and composing with the structure morphism of the covered object keeps that
property. -/
public theorem exists_flatLocallyOfFinitePresentation_refinement
    (X : AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver B S hS)
    (hX : Flat ((Over.post B.inclusion).obj X).hom ∧
      LocallyOfFinitePresentation ((Over.post B.inclusion).obj X).hom)
    (T : Sieve X) (hT : T ∈ AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.topology B S hS X) :
    ∃ R : Presieve X, R ≤ T.arrows ∧
      Sieve.generate R ∈ AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.topology B S hS X ∧
      ∀ ⦃Y : AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver B S hS⦄ (f : Y ⟶ X), R f →
        Flat ((Over.post B.inclusion).obj Y).hom ∧
          LocallyOfFinitePresentation ((Over.post B.inclusion).obj Y).hom := by
  rw [← overFppfPrecoverage_toGrothendieck B S hS] at hT
  obtain ⟨R, hR, hRT⟩ :=
    Precoverage.mem_toGrothendieck_iff_of_isStableUnderComposition.mp hT
  refine ⟨R, hRT, ?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [← overFppfPrecoverage_toGrothendieck B S hS]
    exact Precoverage.generate_mem_toGrothendieck hR
  · intro Y f hf
    exact flat_lfp_of_comp B S hS f (flat_lfp_leg_of_mem_overFppfPrecoverage B S hS hR f hf) hX

/-- **A member of a selected covering of `S` itself is flat and locally of finite presentation
over `S`.**  A selected covering is an fppf covering, so its legs are flat and locally of finite
presentation, and the structure morphism of the covered object is an isomorphism. -/
public theorem flat_locallyOfFinitePresentation_of_bigFppfOver_isCovering
    (E : Covering (AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver B S hS))
    (hE : IsIso ((Over.post B.inclusion).obj E.1).hom)
    (hcov : AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.IsCovering B S hS E) (i : E.2.I₀) :
    Flat ((Over.post B.inclusion).obj (E.2.X i)).hom ∧
      LocallyOfFinitePresentation ((Over.post B.inclusion).obj (E.2.X i)).hom := by
  have hmem : E.2.presieve₀ ∈ overFppfPrecoverage B S hS E.1 := by
    have h := hcov.1
    rw [AlgebraicGeometry.IsFppfCovering, Precoverage.mem_comap_iff,
      ← PreZeroHypercover.presieve₀_map] at h
    rw [Precoverage.mem_comap_iff, ← PreZeroHypercover.presieve₀_map]
    exact h
  refine flat_lfp_of_comp B S hS (E.2.f i)
    (flat_lfp_leg_of_mem_overFppfPrecoverage B S hS hmem (E.2.f i)
      (Presieve.ofArrows.mk i)) ?_
  let : IsIso ((Over.post B.inclusion).obj E.1).hom := hE
  exact ⟨inferInstance, inferInstance⟩

end Precoverages

/-! ### Vanishing of the cokernel of a locally surjective morphism of abelian sheaves -/

/-- **A sheaf cokernel has no sections where the morphism is surjective on sections, provided
covering sieves can be refined to stay inside the class of such objects.**

The quotient map onto the cokernel is an epimorphism of sheaves, hence locally surjective, so a
section of the cokernel over `X` lifts to the target on a covering of `X`; refining that
covering to one inside the class, the lift is itself an image, and the composite into the
cokernel is zero.  A locally zero section of a sheaf is zero. -/
public theorem subsingleton_cokernel_val_obj_of_surjective
    {C : Type (u + 1)} [Category.{u} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}
    [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{u}] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
    {A₁ A₂ : Sheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{u}} (ψ : A₁ ⟶ A₂) (Q : C → Prop)
    (hQ : ∀ Y, Q Y → ∀ T : Sieve Y, T ∈ J Y →
      ∃ R : Presieve Y, R ≤ T.arrows ∧ Sieve.generate R ∈ J Y ∧
        ∀ ⦃Z⦄ (f : Z ⟶ Y), R f → Q Z)
    (hψ : ∀ Y, Q Y → Function.Surjective (ψ.hom.app (op Y)))
    (X : C) (hX : Q X) :
    Subsingleton ((cokernel ψ).obj.obj (op X)) := by
  have hzeroComp : ∀ (Z : C) (v : A₁.obj.obj (op Z)),
      (cokernel.π ψ).hom.app (op Z) (ψ.hom.app (op Z) v) = 0 := by
    intro Z v
    have h0 : (sheafToPresheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{u}).map ψ ≫
        (sheafToPresheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{u}).map (cokernel.π ψ) = 0 := by
      rw [← Functor.map_comp, cokernel.condition, Functor.map_zero]
    have h1 := congrArg (fun α : A₁.obj ⟶ (cokernel ψ).obj => α.app (op Z)) h0
    simp only [NatTrans.comp_app] at h1
    simpa using ConcreteCategory.congr_hom h1 v
  have hsurj : Sheaf.IsLocallySurjective (cokernel.π ψ) := by
    rw [Sheaf.isLocallySurjective_iff_epi']
    infer_instance
  refine subsingleton_of_forall_eq 0 fun s => ?_
  obtain ⟨R, hRle, hRmem, hRQ⟩ := hQ X hX
    (Presheaf.imageSieve (cokernel.π ψ).hom s)
    (Presheaf.imageSieve_mem (J := J) _ s)
  refine (cokernel ψ).isSeparated X (Sieve.generate R) hRmem s 0 ?_
  rintro Y f ⟨Z, g, h, hh, rfl⟩
  obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ := hRle _ _ hh
  obtain ⟨v, hv⟩ := hψ Z (hRQ h hh) t
  have hzero : (cokernel ψ).obj.map h.op s = 0 := by
    rw [← ht, ← hv, hzeroComp]
  simp only [op_comp, Functor.map_comp, ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, hzero, map_zero]

/-! ### Parasiticity of the kernel and the cokernel -/

section Parasitic

variable (B : AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)
  [HasSheafify (AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.topology B S hS) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [(AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.topology B S hS).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  {𝒪 : Sheaf (AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.topology B S hS) RingCat.{u}}
  {F G : SheafOfModules.{u} 𝒪}

/-- Sections of the underlying abelian sheaf of a sheaf of modules over a fixed object. -/
private abbrev sectionsFunctor (X : AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver B S hS) :
    SheafOfModules.{u} 𝒪 ⥤ AddCommGrpCat.{u} :=
  SheafOfModules.toSheaf 𝒪 ⋙
    sheafToPresheaf (AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.topology B S hS) AddCommGrpCat.{u} ⋙
      (evaluation (AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ AddCommGrpCat.{u}).obj (op X)

omit [HasSheafify (AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.topology B S hS) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [(AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.topology B S hS).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}] in
/-- **The kernel has no sections over an object where the morphism is an isomorphism on
sections.** -/
private theorem subsingleton_kernel_val_obj (φ : F ⟶ G)
    (X : AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver B S hS) (hX : IsIso (φ.val.app (op X))) :
    Subsingleton ((kernel φ).val.obj (op X)) := by
  have hmono : Mono ((sectionsFunctor B S hS X).map φ) :=
    ConcreteCategory.mono_of_injective _
      (ConcreteCategory.bijective_of_isIso (φ.val.app (op X))).injective
  have hz : IsZero ((sectionsFunctor B S hS X).obj (kernel φ)) :=
    (isZero_kernel_of_mono ((sectionsFunctor B S hS X).map φ)).of_iso
      (PreservesKernel.iso (sectionsFunctor B S hS X) φ)
  exact AddCommGrpCat.subsingleton_of_isZero hz

/-- **The cokernel has no sections over an object flat and locally of finite presentation over
`S` when the morphism is an isomorphism on sections over every such object.** -/
private theorem subsingleton_cokernel_val_obj (φ : F ⟶ G)
    (hφ : ∀ Y : AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver B S hS,
      Flat ((Over.post B.inclusion).obj Y).hom →
      LocallyOfFinitePresentation ((Over.post B.inclusion).obj Y).hom →
      IsIso (φ.val.app (op Y)))
    (X : AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver B S hS)
    (hX : Flat ((Over.post B.inclusion).obj X).hom ∧
      LocallyOfFinitePresentation ((Over.post B.inclusion).obj X).hom) :
    Subsingleton ((cokernel φ).val.obj (op X)) := by
  have habelian :
      Subsingleton ((cokernel ((SheafOfModules.toSheaf 𝒪).map φ)).obj.obj (op X)) := by
    refine subsingleton_cokernel_val_obj_of_surjective ((SheafOfModules.toSheaf 𝒪).map φ)
      (fun Y ↦ Flat ((Over.post B.inclusion).obj Y).hom ∧
        LocallyOfFinitePresentation ((Over.post B.inclusion).obj Y).hom)
      (fun Y hY T hT ↦ exists_flatLocallyOfFinitePresentation_refinement B S hS Y hY T hT)
      (fun Y hY ↦ ?_) X hX
    have := hφ Y hY.1 hY.2
    exact (ConcreteCategory.bijective_of_isIso (φ.val.app (op Y))).surjective
  have hiso : (sectionsFunctor B S hS X).obj (cokernel φ) ≅
      (cokernel ((SheafOfModules.toSheaf 𝒪).map φ)).obj.obj (op X) :=
    (sheafToPresheaf (AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.topology B S hS) AddCommGrpCat.{u} ⋙
      (evaluation (AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ
        AddCommGrpCat.{u}).obj (op X)).mapIso
      (PreservesCokernel.iso (SheafOfModules.toSheaf 𝒪) φ)
  exact hiso.addCommGroupIsoToAddEquiv.toEquiv.subsingleton

variable [HasExt.{w} (Sheaf (AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.topology B S hS) AddCommGrpCat.{u})]

omit [HasSheafify (AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.topology B S hS) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [(AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.topology B S hS).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [HasExt.{w} (Sheaf (AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.topology B S hS) AddCommGrpCat.{u})] in
/-- **The kernel of a morphism which is an isomorphism on sections over every object flat and
locally of finite presentation over `S` is parasitic for the fppf topology.** -/
public theorem isParasiticFor_kernel_of_isIso_sections (φ : F ⟶ G)
    (hφ : ∀ Y : AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver B S hS,
      Flat ((Over.post B.inclusion).obj Y).hom →
      LocallyOfFinitePresentation ((Over.post B.inclusion).obj Y).hom →
      IsIso (φ.val.app (op Y))) :
    AlgebraicGeometry.IsParasiticFor S (Over.post B.inclusion)
      (AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.IsCovering B S hS) (kernel φ).val := by
  intro E hE hcov i
  obtain ⟨h1, h2⟩ :=
    flat_locallyOfFinitePresentation_of_bigFppfOver_isCovering B S hS E hE hcov i
  exact subsingleton_kernel_val_obj B S hS φ (E.2.X i) (hφ (E.2.X i) h1 h2)

omit [HasExt.{w} (Sheaf (AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.topology B S hS) AddCommGrpCat.{u})] in
/-- **The cokernel of a morphism which is an isomorphism on sections over every object flat and
locally of finite presentation over `S` is parasitic for the fppf topology.** -/
public theorem isParasiticFor_cokernel_of_isIso_sections (φ : F ⟶ G)
    (hφ : ∀ Y : AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver B S hS,
      Flat ((Over.post B.inclusion).obj Y).hom →
      LocallyOfFinitePresentation ((Over.post B.inclusion).obj Y).hom →
      IsIso (φ.val.app (op Y))) :
    AlgebraicGeometry.IsParasiticFor S (Over.post B.inclusion)
      (AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.IsCovering B S hS) (cokernel φ).val := by
  intro E hE hcov i
  exact subsingleton_cokernel_val_obj B S hS φ hφ (E.2.X i)
    (flat_locallyOfFinitePresentation_of_bigFppfOver_isCovering B S hS E hE hcov i)

/-- **A morphism of sheaves of `𝒪`-modules on the big fppf site over `S` which is an isomorphism
on sections over every object flat and locally of finite presentation over `S` induces
isomorphisms `H^p(U, ℱ) → H^p(U, 𝒢)` at every such object `U`, in every degree.**

This is the step of [Stacks, Tag 0756] which rests on [Stacks, Tag 0755], with the parasitic
hypotheses of `AlgebraicGeometry.bigFppfCohomology_map_bijective_of_isParasiticFor` supplied as
theorems: they follow from the sectionwise isomorphism hypothesis by
`AlgebraicGeometry.isParasiticFor_kernel_of_isIso_sections` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.isParasiticFor_cokernel_of_isIso_sections`.

Read at the identity chart of `U_τ`, hypothesis (2) of [Stacks, Tag 0756] — that the canonical
map `g^*_{τ,small}(𝒢|_{S_τ}) → 𝒢|_{U_τ}` be an isomorphism for every flat, locally finitely
presented `g : U → S` — says exactly that the comparison map is an isomorphism on sections over
`U`, which is the hypothesis here; the source's proof uses its hypotheses (1) and (2) only
through that.

The comparison pair `ℱ = (𝒢|_{S_τ})^a` with its canonical map is constructed in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Descent/Parasitic/FlatCohomologyCounit.lean`, and the
identification of the left-hand side `H^p(U, ℱ)` with the small-site cohomology
`H^p(U, 𝒢|_{U_τ})`, which is the conclusion of 0756, is established at `τ = Zariski` and
`U = S` by `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.zariskiSmallSiteCohomologyAddEquiv` in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Descent/Parasitic/FlatCohomologySmallSiteComparison.lean`. -/
public theorem bigFppfCohomology_map_bijective_of_isIso_sections (φ : F ⟶ G)
    (hφ : ∀ Y : AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver B S hS,
      Flat ((Over.post B.inclusion).obj Y).hom →
